    "id": "jetcoat-premium",
    "name": "Jetcoat Premium Driveway Sealer",
    "category": "Filled Asphalt Emulsion",
    "badge": "Best for Rough Surfaces",
    "amazonUrl": "",
    "pros": [
      "Thick, filled formula suited to weathered, open-textured asphalt",
      "Good value per pail compared with flagship lines",
      "Easy to find online and in many hardware stores",
      "Dries to a uniform matte black"
    ],
    "cons": [
      "Long-life wording on the pail is a tier name, not a guarantee of years between coats",
      "Thick body takes more effort to spread with a brush"
    ],
    "bottomLine": "A solid mid-priced choice for older driveways that need filler as much as they need a fresh black coat.",
    "description": "Jetcoat Premium is a filled asphalt emulsion aimed at driveways that have been neglected for a few seasons. Its heavier body is the selling point: on asphalt where the fine material between stones has washed out, a thin sealer simply disappears into the voids, while a filled product sits up on the surface and closes some of that texture. Owners commonly report that it covers rough driveways better than budget pails, and that it looks good after one coat on surfaces that only needed a refresh. As with every product here, read the years printed on the front as a product tier. How long the coat actually lasts depends on traffic, sun, snowplow damage and how well the surface was cleaned. Confirm the formula on the specific pail you buy, because coal tar products are banned in several states and cities and you should know exactly what you are putting down. For a value-minded owner with an aging driveway, this is a reasonable middle ground."
  },
  {
    "id": "henry-blacktop-sealer",
    "name": "Henry Asphalt Driveway Filler & Sealer",
    "category": "Asphalt Emulsion + Filler",
    "badge": "Best Budget",
