          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most asphalt driveways, Latex-ite Airport Grade is the pail to buy: filled, polymer-modified, easy to work and sold almost everywhere. Spend more on Black Jack Drive-Maxx 1000 if the surface is smooth and the finish matters to you, and spend less on Henry or Gardner if the driveway was sealed recently and only needs a refresh.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The product matters less than the prep. Clean the surface completely, fill the cracks properly, apply two thin coats in warm, dry weather, and keep cars off it for two days. Do that every two to three years, not every year, and almost any reputable sealer will keep a sound driveway looking and performing well.
          </p>
